{"batchcomplete":"","continue":{"gsroffset":10,"continue":"gsroffset||"},"query":{"pages":{"115891685":{"pageid":115891685,"ns":6,"title":"File:Debussy crater MESSENGER mosaic.jpg","index":10,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":657925,"width":1040,"height":1048,"thumburl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/56/Debussy_crater_MESSENGER_mosaic.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","thumbwidth":1600,"thumbheight":1612,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/56/Debussy_crater_MESSENGER_mosaic.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1600,"height":1612},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/56/Debussy_crater_MESSENGER_mosaic.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Debussy_crater_MESSENGER_mosaic.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=115891685","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2022-03-08 03:22:20","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"Debussy crater MESSENGER mosaic","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"Debussy (crater)|PD NASA|Ray systems|Photos of Mercury by MESSENGER","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"Date: October 6, 2008\n<p>Instrument: Narrow Angle Camera (NAC) of the Mercury Dual Imaging System (MDIS)\nResolution: 500 meters/pixel (0.31 miles/pixel)\nScale: The diameter of Debussy is 85 kilometers (53 miles)\nProjection: This image is a portion of the global Mercury mosaic. It is shown in an orthographic projection.\n</p>\nOf Interest: This central-peak crater naturally draws attention because of its prominent rays, which extend hundreds of kilometers across the planet. Until receiving its official name of Debussy in March 2010, this crater had been known only as \"feature A\" in Earth-based radar images of Mercury. Debussy's extensive system of rays makes it a prominent, bright feature on Mercury's surface at both visible and radar wavelengths, and it was identified from early Earth-based radar observations long before the collection of spacecraft images of the crater. Appropriately, radar astronomer John K. Harmon was involved in proposing the name Debussy, as well as the name Hokusai for another spectacularly rayed crater discovered by radar. This crater's name honors Claude Debussy (1862-1918), a French composer. The first spacecraft images of Debussy were obtained during MESSENGER's second flyby of Mercury, revealing Debussy and its hundreds of miles of rays in unprecedented detail.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2010-07-06","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://messenger.jhuapl.edu/Explore/Science-Images-Database/gallery-image-385.html\">DEBUSSY AND ITS HUNDREDS OF MILES OF RAYS</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"NASA/Johns Hopkins University Applied Physics Laboratory/Carnegie Institution of Washington","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]},"28487739":{"pageid":28487739,"ns":6,"title":"File:MESSENGER first photo of unseen side of Mercury (super high resolution).jpg","index":8,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":6512573,"width":8145,"height":9305,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/MESSENGER_first_photo_of_unseen_side_of_Mercury_%28super_high_resolution%29.jpg/1920px-MESSENGER_first_photo_of_unseen_side_of_Mercury_%28super_high_resolution%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1600,"thumbheight":1828,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/MESSENGER_first_photo_of_unseen_side_of_Mercury_%28super_high_resolution%29.jpg/3840px-MESSENGER_first_photo_of_unseen_side_of_Mercury_%28super_high_resolution%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/MESSENGER_first_photo_of_unseen_side_of_Mercury_%28super_high_resolution%29.jpg/1920px-MESSENGER_first_photo_of_unseen_side_of_Mercury_%28super_high_resolution%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1600,"height":1828,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/MESSENGER_first_photo_of_unseen_side_of_Mercury_%28super_high_resolution%29.jpg/3840px-MESSENGER_first_photo_of_unseen_side_of_Mercury_%28super_high_resolution%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e4/MESSENGER_first_photo_of_unseen_side_of_Mercury_%28super_high_resolution%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MESSENGER_first_photo_of_unseen_side_of_Mercury_(super_high_resolution).jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=28487739","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2013-09-23 02:10:12","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"MESSENGER first photo of unseen side of Mercury (super high resolution)","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"PD NASA|Surface features of Mercury|Photos of Mercury by MESSENGER","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"This global mosaic of Mercury, consisting of 87 MDIS Narrow-angle Camera images, shows features of the planet not seen during the Mariner 10 flybys of the 1970s. These were taken during the January 14, 2008, flyby of Mercury by the MESSENGER spacecraft, and taken at a distance of between 17,484 and 20,790 km (10,864 and 12,918 mi) from the planet. The approximate resolution of this mosaic is 550 m/pixel.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2008-01-14","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.gishbartimes.org/2008/07/mercury-mosaics-from-messenger.html\">http://www.gishbartimes.org/2008/07/mercury-mosaics-from-messenger.html</a> (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://pirlwww.lpl.arizona.edu/%7Eperry/Messenger/Global_mosaic1.jpg\">image link</a>)","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NASA\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:NASA\">NASA</a>/<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Applied_Physics_Laboratory\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Applied Physics Laboratory\">JHUAPL</a>/<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carnegie_Institution_for_Science\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Carnegie Institution for Science\">CIW</a>/Jason Perry","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]},"23843231":{"pageid":23843231,"ns":6,"title":"File:Mercury Globe-MESSENGER mosaic centered at 0degN-0degE.jpg","index":6,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":903538,"width":2147,"height":2147,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Mercury_Globe-MESSENGER_mosaic_centered_at_0degN-0degE.jpg/1920px-Mercury_Globe-MESSENGER_mosaic_centered_at_0degN-0degE.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1600,"thumbheight":1600,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3f/Mercury_Globe-MESSENGER_mosaic_centered_at_0degN-0degE.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Mercury_Globe-MESSENGER_mosaic_centered_at_0degN-0degE.jpg/1920px-Mercury_Globe-MESSENGER_mosaic_centered_at_0degN-0degE.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1600,"height":1600,"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3f/Mercury_Globe-MESSENGER_mosaic_centered_at_0degN-0degE.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3f/Mercury_Globe-MESSENGER_mosaic_centered_at_0degN-0degE.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mercury_Globe-MESSENGER_mosaic_centered_at_0degN-0degE.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=23843231","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2013-01-14 09:33:55","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"Mercury Globe-MESSENGER mosaic centered at 0degN-0degE","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"PD NASA|Images with annotations|Files with derivative versions|Images with 10+ annotations|Photos of Mercury by MESSENGER","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"This image shows an orthographic projection of this global mosaic centered at 0\u00b0N, 0\u00b0E. The rayed crater Debussy can be seen towards the bottom of the globe and the peak-ring basin Rachmaninoff can be seen towards the eastern edge.\nRelease Date: November 29, 2011","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2013-01-14 03:30:39","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"NASA <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" data-mw-original-href=\"http://www.nasa.gov/mission_pages/messenger/multimedia/messenger_orbit_image20111129_1.html\" href=\"https://www.nasa.gov/mission_pages/messenger/multimedia/messenger_orbit_image20111129_1.html\">[1]</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"NASA/JHUAPL","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]},"143455173":{"pageid":143455173,"ns":6,"title":"File:Mercury MESSENGER MDIS Basemap BDR Mosaic Global 32ppd.jpg","index":3,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":22564775,"width":11520,"height":5760,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_BDR_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg/1920px-Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_BDR_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1600,"thumbheight":800,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_BDR_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg/3840px-Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_BDR_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_BDR_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg/1920px-Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_BDR_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1600,"height":800,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_BDR_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg/3840px-Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_BDR_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c8/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_BDR_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_BDR_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=143455173","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2024-01-03 04:02:22","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"Mercury MESSENGER MDIS Basemap BDR Mosaic Global 32ppd","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"PD USGS|Maps of Mercury","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"The Map Projected Basemap RDR (BDR) data set consists of a global monochrome map of reflectance at a resolution of 256 pixels per degree (~166 m/p). This edition, version 1, was released May 6, 2016 to the Planetary Data System (PDS) MESSENGER archive. It is compiled using NAC or WAC 750-nm images from any campaign that best fit the intended illumination geometry or low emission angle and incidence angle near 74\u00b0. It is controlled and projected onto a global digital elevation model. It uses a Kasseleinin-Shkuratov photometric model, whose parameters are the same for any given wavelength band across all MESSENGER end-of-mission map data products.\nThis mosaic contains data acquired by the MErcury Surface, Space ENvironment, GEochemistry and Ranging (MESSENGER) Mercury Dual Imaging System (MDIS) instrument.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2016-05-06","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://astrogeology.usgs.gov/search/map/Mercury/Messenger/Global/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_BDR_Mosaic_Global_166m\">https://astrogeology.usgs.gov/search/map/Mercury/Messenger/Global/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_BDR_Mosaic_Global_166m</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"Planetary Data System, Applied Coherent Technology Corporation","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]},"143455174":{"pageid":143455174,"ns":6,"title":"File:Mercury MESSENGER MDIS Basemap EnhancedColor Mosaic Global 32ppd.jpg","index":5,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":30106303,"width":11520,"height":5760,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_EnhancedColor_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg/1920px-Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_EnhancedColor_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1600,"thumbheight":800,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_EnhancedColor_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg/3840px-Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_EnhancedColor_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_EnhancedColor_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg/1920px-Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_EnhancedColor_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1600,"height":800,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_EnhancedColor_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg/3840px-Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_EnhancedColor_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/41/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_EnhancedColor_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_EnhancedColor_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=143455174","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2024-01-03 04:02:22","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"Mercury MESSENGER MDIS Basemap EnhancedColor Mosaic Global 32ppd","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"PD USGS|Maps of Mercury","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"This mosaic shows Mercury's surface in \"enhanced color,\" a term used to describe a color scheme created to emphasize color differences on Mercury's surface. This is not what Mercury would look like to the human eye, but rather by applying mathematical analysis to MESSENGER images, color differences on Mercury's surface can be accentuated beyond those visible to a person. This view uses a global mosaic with 430, 750, and 1000 nm bands and places the second principal component, the first principal component, and the 430/1000 ratio in the red, green, and blue channels respectively.\nThis mosaic contains data acquired by the MErcury Surface, Space ENvironment, GEochemistry and Ranging (MESSENGER) Mercury Dual Imaging System (MDIS) instrument.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2016-05-13","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://astrogeology.usgs.gov/search/map/Mercury/Messenger/Global/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_EnhancedColor_Mosaic_Global_665m\">https://astrogeology.usgs.gov/search/map/Mercury/Messenger/Global/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_EnhancedColor_Mosaic_Global_665m</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"Johns Hopkins Applied Physics Laboratory, Applied Coherent Technology Corporation","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]},"143482614":{"pageid":143482614,"ns":6,"title":"File:Mercury MESSENGER MDIS Basemap MD3Color Mosaic Global 32ppd.jpg","index":2,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":17351889,"width":11520,"height":5760,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_MD3Color_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg/1920px-Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_MD3Color_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1600,"thumbheight":800,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_MD3Color_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg/3840px-Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_MD3Color_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_MD3Color_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg/1920px-Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_MD3Color_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1600,"height":800,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_MD3Color_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg/3840px-Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_MD3Color_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/62/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_MD3Color_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_MD3Color_Mosaic_Global_32ppd.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=143482614","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2024-01-03 19:40:59","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"Mercury MESSENGER MDIS Basemap MD3Color Mosaic Global 32ppd","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"PD USGS|Maps of Mercury","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"This mosaic shows Mercury's colors as viewed by placing images from MESSENGER's 1000 nm, 750 nm, and 430 nm narrow-band filters in the red, green, and blue channel respectively. This is not what Mercury would look like to the human eye, but rather by using a wider range of wavelengths, color differences on Mercury's surface can be accentuated beyond those visible to a person. The projection defined is Simple Cylindrical centered on 0\u00b0 latitude and 0\u00b0 longitude.\n<p>The 3-color Map Projected Multispectral RDR (MD3) data set consists of a mosaicked global color map of 3-color image sets, as reflectance corrected to i = 30\u00ba, e = 0\u00ba, and g = 30\u00ba sampled at a scale of 128 pixels per degree, compiled from images taken as a part of the regional 3-color map campaign. This is version 1 of the map, delivered at end of mission. Instead of the value from any single image being used at a particular pixel location in a given wavelength band, the value used is the average from all of the images at that location where criteria for image scale, photometric geometry, and detector temperature are met.\n</p><p>This mosaic contains data acquired by the MErcury Surface, Space ENvironment, GEochemistry and Ranging (MESSENGER) Mercury Dual Imaging System (MDIS) instrument.\n</p>\nNOTE: This image, from the \"Maximum Size (jpg)\" link, is actually grayscale, not in color.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2016-05-13","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://astrogeology.usgs.gov/search/map/Mercury/Messenger/Global/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_MD3Color_Mosaic_Global_665m\">https://astrogeology.usgs.gov/search/map/Mercury/Messenger/Global/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_MD3Color_Mosaic_Global_665m</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"Johns Hopkins Applied Physics Laboratory, Applied Coherent Technology Corporation","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]},"143482638":{"pageid":143482638,"ns":6,"title":"File:Mercury MESSENGER MDIS Basemap MD3Color Mosaic Global 665m.tif","index":4,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":796539539,"width":23040,"height":11520,"pagecount":1,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_MD3Color_Mosaic_Global_665m.tif/lossy-page1-1920px-Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_MD3Color_Mosaic_Global_665m.tif.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1600,"thumbheight":800,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_MD3Color_Mosaic_Global_665m.tif/lossy-page1-3840px-Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_MD3Color_Mosaic_Global_665m.tif.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_MD3Color_Mosaic_Global_665m.tif/lossy-page1-1920px-Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_MD3Color_Mosaic_Global_665m.tif.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1600,"height":800,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_MD3Color_Mosaic_Global_665m.tif/lossy-page1-3840px-Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_MD3Color_Mosaic_Global_665m.tif.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e3/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_MD3Color_Mosaic_Global_665m.tif?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_MD3Color_Mosaic_Global_665m.tif","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=143482638","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2024-01-03 19:41:39","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"Mercury MESSENGER MDIS Basemap MD3Color Mosaic Global 665m","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"PD USGS|Large images|Maps of Mercury","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"This mosaic shows Mercury's colors as viewed by placing images from MESSENGER's 1000 nm, 750 nm, and 430 nm narrow-band filters in the red, green, and blue channel respectively. This is not what Mercury would look like to the human eye, but rather by using a wider range of wavelengths, color differences on Mercury's surface can be accentuated beyond those visible to a person. The projection defined is Simple Cylindrical centered on 0\u00b0 latitude and 0\u00b0 longitude.\n<p>The 3-color Map Projected Multispectral RDR (MD3) data set consists of a mosaicked global color map of 3-color image sets, as reflectance corrected to i = 30\u00ba, e = 0\u00ba, and g = 30\u00ba sampled at a scale of 128 pixels per degree, compiled from images taken as a part of the regional 3-color map campaign. This is version 1 of the map, delivered at end of mission. Instead of the value from any single image being used at a particular pixel location in a given wavelength band, the value used is the average from all of the images at that location where criteria for image scale, photometric geometry, and detector temperature are met.\n</p>\nThis mosaic contains data acquired by the MErcury Surface, Space ENvironment, GEochemistry and Ranging (MESSENGER) Mercury Dual Imaging System (MDIS) instrument.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2016-05-13","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://astrogeology.usgs.gov/search/map/Mercury/Messenger/Global/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_MD3Color_Mosaic_Global_665m\">https://astrogeology.usgs.gov/search/map/Mercury/Messenger/Global/Mercury_MESSENGER_MDIS_Basemap_MD3Color_Mosaic_Global_665m</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"Johns Hopkins Applied Physics Laboratory, Applied Coherent Technology Corporation","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]},"31184338":{"pageid":31184338,"ns":6,"title":"File:Mercury global map 2013-05-14 bright.png","index":7,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":14284018,"width":6132,"height":3066,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Mercury_global_map_2013-05-14_bright.png/1920px-Mercury_global_map_2013-05-14_bright.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1600,"thumbheight":800,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Mercury_global_map_2013-05-14_bright.png/3840px-Mercury_global_map_2013-05-14_bright.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Mercury_global_map_2013-05-14_bright.png/1920px-Mercury_global_map_2013-05-14_bright.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1600,"height":800,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Mercury_global_map_2013-05-14_bright.png/3840px-Mercury_global_map_2013-05-14_bright.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f2/Mercury_global_map_2013-05-14_bright.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mercury_global_map_2013-05-14_bright.png","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=31184338","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2016-03-18 02:36:51","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"Mercury global map 2013-05-14 bright","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"PD NASA|Retouched pictures|Images with annotations|Images with 10+ annotations|Photos of Mercury by MESSENGER|Maps of Mercury","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"At the very end of 2012, MESSENGER obtained the final image needed to view 100% of Mercury's surface under daylight conditions. The mosaics shown here cover all of Mercury's surface and were produced by using the monochrome mosaic released by NASA's Planetary Data System (PDS) on March 8, 2013, as the base. The full resolution mosaics are available for download on MESSENGER's Global Mosaics webpage.\n<p>To fill the area near the north pole, the PDS product was trimmed northward of 83\u00b0N and an average mosaic that extended from 82.5\u00b0N to 90\u00b0N was used, averaging the 0.5\u00b0 latitude overlap between the PDS mosaic and the average north polar mosaic. To fill the area near the south pole, the PDS product was trimmed southward of 85.5\u00b0S and an average mosaic that extended from 85\u00b0S to 90\u00b0S was used, again averaging the 0.5\u00b0 latitude overlap. Any remaining gaps in the global mosaic were filled by using images obtained in support of the high-incidence imaging campaign.\n</p>\nThis image is a brightness-corrected version of the original (<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mercury_-_complete_mono_basemap_2500mpp_equirectangular.png\" title=\"File:Mercury - complete mono basemap 2500mpp equirectangular.png\">Mercury - complete mono basemap 2500mpp equirectangular.png</a>). Brightness levels were tuned from [0 - 255] to [30 - 180] for increase of contrast.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2013-05-31","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"http://messenger.jhuapl.edu/the_mission/mosaics.html\">http://messenger.jhuapl.edu/the_mission/mosaics.html</a> <br>NASA photojournal page: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" data-mw-original-href=\"http://photojournal.jpl.nasa.gov/catalog/PIA17230\" href=\"https://photojournal.jpl.nasa.gov/catalog/PIA17230\">http://photojournal.jpl.nasa.gov/catalog/PIA17230</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"NASA","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]},"33575210":{"pageid":33575210,"ns":6,"title":"File:Mercury map by MESSENGER global mosaic enhancedcolor over completebasemap.png","index":1,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":24761845,"width":4096,"height":2048,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Mercury_map_by_MESSENGER_global_mosaic_enhancedcolor_over_completebasemap.png/1920px-Mercury_map_by_MESSENGER_global_mosaic_enhancedcolor_over_completebasemap.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1600,"thumbheight":800,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Mercury_map_by_MESSENGER_global_mosaic_enhancedcolor_over_completebasemap.png/3840px-Mercury_map_by_MESSENGER_global_mosaic_enhancedcolor_over_completebasemap.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Mercury_map_by_MESSENGER_global_mosaic_enhancedcolor_over_completebasemap.png/1920px-Mercury_map_by_MESSENGER_global_mosaic_enhancedcolor_over_completebasemap.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1600,"height":800,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Mercury_map_by_MESSENGER_global_mosaic_enhancedcolor_over_completebasemap.png/3840px-Mercury_map_by_MESSENGER_global_mosaic_enhancedcolor_over_completebasemap.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d3/Mercury_map_by_MESSENGER_global_mosaic_enhancedcolor_over_completebasemap.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mercury_map_by_MESSENGER_global_mosaic_enhancedcolor_over_completebasemap.png","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=33575210","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2014-06-25 15:06:08","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"Mercury map by MESSENGER global mosaic enhancedcolor over completebasemap","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"PD NASA|Photos of Mercury by MESSENGER|Maps of Mercury","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"This colorful view of Mercury is similar to that used to generate this movie [23MB, 6.5MB] of Mercury as a spinning globe, and these two individual views (centered at 140\u00b0E and 320\u00b0E) of the innermost planet. The enhanced color view is overlaid on the global monochrome base map, which is available for download here.\n<p>The enhanced color was produced by using images from the color base map imaging campaign during MESSENGER's primary mission. These colors are not what Mercury would look like to the human eye, but rather the colors enhance the chemical, mineralogical, and physical differences between the rocks that make up Mercury's surface. This specific color combination places the second principal component in the red channel, the first principal component in the green channel, and the ratio of the 430 nm/1000 nm filters in the blue channel.\n</p><p>Instrument: Wide Angle Camera (WAC) of the Mercury Dual Imaging System (MDIS)\nCenter Latitude: 0\u00b0\nCenter Longitude: 180\u00b0 E\nMap Projection: Simple cylindrical projection\nResolution: 3.74 km/pixel\n</p>\nScale: Mercury's diameter is 4880 kilometers (3030 miles)","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2013-07-18","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"http://messenger.jhuapl.edu/gallery/sciencePhotos/image.php?image_id=1226\">http://messenger.jhuapl.edu/gallery/sciencePhotos/image.php?image_id=1226</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"NASA/Johns Hopkins University Applied Physics Laboratory/Carnegie Institution of Washington","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]},"116187946":{"pageid":116187946,"ns":6,"title":"File:N\u0101wah\u012b crater MESSENGER NAC mosaic.jpg","index":9,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":564581,"width":2593,"height":1269,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/N%C4%81wah%C4%AB_crater_MESSENGER_NAC_mosaic.jpg/1920px-N%C4%81wah%C4%AB_crater_MESSENGER_NAC_mosaic.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1600,"thumbheight":783,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c8/N%C4%81wah%C4%AB_crater_MESSENGER_NAC_mosaic.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/N%C4%81wah%C4%AB_crater_MESSENGER_NAC_mosaic.jpg/1920px-N%C4%81wah%C4%AB_crater_MESSENGER_NAC_mosaic.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1600,"height":783,"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c8/N%C4%81wah%C4%AB_crater_MESSENGER_NAC_mosaic.jpg?